17,7633,54934,16,4999,16,7257,87,313,320,16,4999,16,7257,87,313,7,16,11,16,7257,87,313,4080,16,11,16,7257,87,313,21621,317,7633,54934,16,4999,16,7287,87,313,320,16,4999,16,7287,87,313,7,16,11,16,7287,87,313,4080,16,11,16,7287,87,313,21621,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThree identical squares are placed side by side to form a rectangle with a perimeter of 104 inches. What is the area, in square inches, of each square?\n\n[asy]\nsize(150);\npair x = (2,0);\ndraw((-1,-1)-- (1,-1)--(1,1)--(-1,1)--cycle);\ndraw((-1,-1)+x-- (1,-1)+x--(1,1)+x--(-1,1)+x--cycle);\ndraw((-1,-1)-x-- (1,-1)-x--(1,1)-x--(-1,1)-x--cycle);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"0496ab804efc04b8a631a06c6e7b04254fdbde9c88e92dad810a49cb21699d49"},"seconds":9.497353076934814,"seed":994727141186010407,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the side length of each square and then find the area of one square.\n\n1. **Identify the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   - When three identical squares are placed side by side, the length of the rectangle is three times the side length of one square, and the width is the side length of one square.\n   - Let the side length of each square be \\( s \\). Then the length of the rectangle is \\( 3s \\) and the width is \\( s \\).\n\n2. **Calculate the perimeter of the rectangle:**\n   - The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by the formula \\( P = 2 \\times (\\text{length} + \\text{width}) \\).\n   - Substituting the dimensions of the rectangle, we get:\n     \\[\n     P = 2 \\times (3s + s) = 2 \\times 4s = 8s\n     \\]\n   - We know the perimeter is 104 inches, so we set up the equation:\n     \\[\n     8s = 104\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( s \\):**\n   \\[\n   s = \\frac{104}{8} = 13\n   \\]\n   - Therefore, the side length of each square is 13 inches.\n\n4. **Calculate the area of one square:**\n   - The area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the formula \\( A = s^2 \\).\n   - Substituting the side length \\( s = 13 \\), we get:\n     \\[\n     A = 13^2 = 169\n     \\]\n\nThe area of each square is \\(\\boxed{169}\\) square inches."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{169}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:517"}
